3.2 
Emergency Hearings 
Requests or motions for an emergency hearing are decided by the Judge.   If the 
matter is a bona fide emergency, the movant shall file the motion for an emergency 
hearing with the Clerk of Court.  The Clerk will e-mail the motion to the JA and the 
Judge will then review the motion to determine if it is an actual emergency and if a 
hearing is warranted.  Opposing Counsel must be given a copy of the motion with 
all attachments. 
 
 
SECTION 4 - PRESENCE OF DEFENDANTS/CRIMINAL CASES 
4.1 
In General 
A defendant’s presence is required at ALL HEARINGS AND CASE 
MANAGEMENT CONFERENCES unless previously waived by the Court or by 
Court order.  However, Counsel are authorized to waive the appearance of their 
clients for routine case management conferences, provided the requirements of 
Section 4.4 are satisfied.  No Court order or approval is required. 
 
4.1.1  Defendant’s In-Person Presence Required At Final Pretrial Conference 
All defendants are required to be present, in person, at all final pretrial conferences. 
Counsel are specifically ordered not to excuse the in-person presence of his or her 
client at the final pretrial conference.  
4.2 
Criminal Cases - Defendants in Custody (in Franklin County Jail) 
Defendants are not automatically transported to the courthouse for routine or non-
evidentiary hearings.  If Counsel wants a defendant transported, a request must be 
made to the Franklin County Jail by calling (850) 670-8500, no later than 24 hours 
before the proceeding.  
 
Defendants are automatically transported to the courthouse for violation of probation 
hearings, final pretrial conferences and trials; no request of the Franklin County Jail 
is required for these proceedings. 
 
 

